@'
from pathlib import Path

path = Path('project_sources/agent_runtime/README.md')
text = path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
marker = '## Unified Release, Drift, and Parity Report\n'
section = '''## Gemini Knowledge Consolidation Evaluation

`tools/evaluate_gemini_knowledge_consolidation.py` is the read-only decision surface for evaluating a consolidated Gemini Knowledge layout without changing the active Gemini target contract. It reuses the lossless source-record, projection-boundary, hash, and recovery primitives from `project_agent_knowledge.py`; candidate outputs are virtual evaluation surfaces rather than generated authority or live attachments.

The stage-7 evaluation in `docs/Gemini_Knowledge_Consolidation_Decision.md` found that the current 28 direct canonical Gemini attachments can be represented losslessly by an 8-file candidate with exact 28/28 source accounting. The current governed decision is **DEFER**, not PROMOTE: no candidate-specific live Gemini retrieval/behavior evidence exists, and #184 remains the separate live-behavior risk tracker. The active Gemini bundle therefore remains on all 28 direct canonical attachments.

Run the static evaluation from the repository root:

```bash
python project_sources/agent_runtime/tools/evaluate_gemini_knowledge_consolidation.py --baseline-commit <tested-sha>
python project_sources/agent_runtime/tools/evaluate_gemini_knowledge_consolidation.py --baseline-commit <tested-sha> --markdown
```

A clean static run with no live evidence intentionally reports `DEFER`. A future `PROMOTE` result requires a specifically identified passing live candidate evidence run and must be invoked with both `--live-evidence-status pass` and `--live-evidence-run <evidence>`. A candidate-specific live failure can be recorded with `--live-evidence-status fail --live-evidence-run <evidence>` and remains `DEFER`; blocking static errors report `REVISE`. None of these evaluation outcomes silently changes `Knowledge_Projection_Manifest.json` or the live Gemini Agent.

The evaluator's fail-closed self-tests are imported by `tests/project_agent_knowledge_selftest.py`, so the existing governed Knowledge self-test command exercises both the canonical projection contract and the consolidation evaluator without adding or changing workflow YAML.

'''
if text.count(marker) != 1:
    raise SystemExit(f'expected one README insertion marker, found {text.count(marker)}')
text = text.replace(marker, section + marker, 1)
old = 'Later issues may consider Gemini runtime knowledge consolidation only after the OpenAI packages and unified release report establish a reviewed parity baseline, and may separately align remaining Supabase `ircore` routing, scenarios, source references, and validation records.'
new = 'Gemini runtime Knowledge consolidation was evaluated by #416 after the OpenAI packages and unified release report established the parity baseline; the current decision is DEFER and the active Gemini target remains on 28 direct canonical attachments. Later work may separately align remaining Supabase `ircore` routing, scenarios, source references, and validation records.'
if text.count(old) != 1:
    raise SystemExit(f'expected one Deferred Work sentence, found {text.count(old)}')
text = text.replace(old, new, 1)
path.write_text(text, encoding='utf-8')
